From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:44:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 003/138] ASoC: cs35l33: Read the H/G headroom from DT

cs35l33_set_hg_data() writes hg_config->hd_rm to HG_HEAD whenever the
"cirrus,hg-algo" sub-node is present, but nothing ever sets hd_rm from
the device tree. The headroom is therefore always forced to 0, replacing
the chip default.

Parse a "cirrus,hd-rm" property so boards can set it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/cs35l33.txt | 3 +++
 sound/soc/codecs/cs35l33.c                          | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/cs35l33.txt b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/cs35l33.txt
index dc5a355d1..552717135 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/cs35l33.txt
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/cs35l33.txt
@@ -58,6 +58,9 @@ Optional properties for the "cirrus,hg-algo" sub-node:
     allowing release condition tracking updates. The number of LRCLK periods
     start at 3 to a maximum of 255.
 
+  - cirrus,hd-rm : Class H/G headroom, 0 to 0x7F. Defaults to 0 when the
+    sub-node is present.
+
   - cirrus,ldo-thld : Configures the signal threshold at which the PWM output
     stage enters LDO operation. Starts as a default value of 50mV for a value
     of 1 and increases with a step size of 50mV to a maximum of 750mV (value of
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l33.c b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l33.c
index e217da124..23ff3d240 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l33.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l33.c
@@ -936,6 +936,8 @@ static int cs35l33_get_hg_data(const struct device_node *np,
 		if (of_property_read_u32(hg, "cirrus,release-rate",
 				&val32) >= 0)
 			hg_config->release_rate = val32;
+		if (of_property_read_u32(hg, "cirrus,hd-rm", &val32) >= 0)
+			hg_config->hd_rm = val32;
 		if (of_property_read_u32(hg, "cirrus,ldo-thld", &val32) >= 0)
 			hg_config->ldo_thld = val32;
 		if (of_property_read_u32(hg, "cirrus,ldo-path-disable",
